{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetR7C1rEzS2ithQjWxPQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now I have all the context I need. Let me summarize the analysis:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order model (Order.kt) has no status field currently\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt:21-34) handles POST /orders\n- InMemoryOrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:15-18) has save/findById methods\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt) lacks findByOrderId method\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt:26-44) creates shipments but doesn't validate order status\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31-37) has existing codes; needs new ones for cancellation\n- GlobalExceptionHandler (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28) converts ApiException to ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Error handling via sealed class ApiException with subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on error envelope structure including error.code\n- Tests clear repositories before each test with @BeforeEach\n- State changes must be verified via separate GET request per testing-and-verification skill\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt - add status: OrderStatus field\n2. OrderController.kt - add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint  \n3. ShipmentRepository.kt - add findByOrderId method\n4. ShipmentController.kt - validate order status before creating shipment\n5. ApiError.kt - add error codes for cancelled order rejection\n6. OrderControllerTest.kt - add comprehensive cancel endpoint tests\n\n**Risks:**\n- Atomicity: all-or-nothing on shipment confirmation check\n- Idempotency: already-cancelled orders must succeed silently\n- Race condition: shipment confirmation between validation and cancellation\n- Must prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class. Create OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. Orders are ACTIVE by default when created.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` that:\n   - Finds the order or throws ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - If already CANCELLED, return the order (idempotent)\n   - If ACTIVE, check all shipments for that order\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with new error code and don't modify anything\n   - Otherwise, set order status to CANCELLED, save it, and cancel all CREATED shipments\n   - Return the cancelled order\n\n3. **InMemoryOrderRepository.kt** - No changes needed; save method works for updates\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to query shipments by order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Before creating a shipment, verify the order exists and is not CANCELLED. If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with error code.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (when trying to create shipment for cancelled order) and `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` (when a confirmed shipment blocks cancellation)\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests covering:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order succeeds and persists (verify via GET)\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order cancels its CREATED shipments\n   - Cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds without changing state\n   - Cancelling fails with 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED (verify via GET that nothing changed)\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n   - Creating a shipment for a cancelled order returns 409\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered using a service layer (OrderService) to handle cancel logic, but this would add unnecessary complexity since the operation is straightforward and the existing controllers directly query repositories. The ticket emphasizes preserving existing architecture, and adding a service layer is an unrelated architectural change.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Happy path - cancel ACTIVE order:*\n- Client: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- Controller: finds Order(orderId=O-1, status=ACTIVE)\n- Controller: queries ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(O-1), gets list of shipments\n- Controller: checks if any have status CONFIRMED\n- Controller: saves Order with status=CANCELLED\n- Controller: for each CREATED shipment, updates to CANCELLED and saves\n- Response: 200 OK with cancelled Order in body\n\n*Idempotent path - cancel CANCELLED order:*\n- Client: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- Controller: finds Order with status=CANCELLED\n- Response: 200 OK with same Order unchanged\n\n*Conflict path - CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancel:*\n- Client: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- Controller: finds Order(status=ACTIVE)\n- Controller: queries shipments, finds at least one with status=CONFIRMED\n- Controller: throws ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED, message)\n- Response: 409 CONFLICT with error envelope\n- Order remains ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n\n*Not found path:*\n- Client: POST /orders/O-99/cancel\n- Controller: repository.findById returns null\n- Controller: throws ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND, message)\n- Response: 404 NOT_FOUND with error envelope\n\n*Create shipment for cancelled order:*\n- Client: POST /shipments with orderId=O-1 (where O-1 is CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController: validates order exists via repository.findById\n- ShipmentController: checks order.status == CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController: throws ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED, message)\n- Response: 409 CONFLICT with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancelsAnActiveOrderAndReturnsIt()` - Asserts POST response body has CANCELLED status, then GETs the order and asserts it's CANCELLED\n2. `cancellationCancelsCreatedShipments()` - Creates order with CREATED shipment, cancels order, GETs shipment and asserts CANCELLED\n3. `cancellingCancelledOrderSucceeds()` - Cancels order twice, both succeed, second response identical to first\n4. `cancelFailsWithConfirmedShipment()` - Creates order with CONFIRMED shipment, POST returns 409 with ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED code, GETs order and asserts still ACTIVE, GETs shipment and asserts still CONFIRMED\n5. `cancellingNonexistentOrderReturns404()` - POST to non-existent order returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n6. `creatingShipmentForCancelledOrderReturns409()` - Cancels order, attempts POST /shipments, returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Starting with the Order model:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1773,"cache_read_input_tokens":21183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1773},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7517c5a9-f734-4f39-9333-2e161584f361","uuid":"629769c9-ca7d-45b6-bd80-3262e1a41522","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:27:48.501Z","request_id":"req_011CetR7BQ8UXdEBBcfqJepN"}
