point. ✅ Necessary for cancel functionality. The endpoint:\n   - Checks order exists (404 if not)\n   - Returns as-is if already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Validates no CONFIRMED shipments (409 if any exist)\n   - Updates order to CANCELLED and saves\n   - Cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Uses proper exception types per API contract\n\n3. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added OrderRepository injection and validation before creating shipment. ✅ Necessary to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId method. ✅ Necessary to query shipments for a given order during cancel operation.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes. ✅ Necessary for new error cases.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 7 new test cases covering all scenarios. ✅ Tests follow existing pattern and verify state via separate GET requests per testing-and-verification skill requirements.\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All requirements implemented and verified.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with order status tracking, atomic validation, and idempotent cancellation\nChanged       Order.kt — added OrderStatus enum and status field to track ACTIVE/CANCELLED state\nChanged       OrderController.kt — added cancel endpoint with shipment confirmation validation and CREATED shipment cancellation\nChanged       ShipmentController.kt — added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\nChanged       ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId method to query shipments by order\nChanged       ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\nChanged       OrderControllerTest.kt — added 7 comprehensive tests covering all cancel scenarios including idempotency, atomicity, and error cases\nTests         `newlyCreatedOrderHasActiveStatus` verifies orders start ACTIVE\nTests         `cancelsAnActiveOrderAndReturnsItWithCancelledStatus` verifies cancel works and persists via separate GET\nTests         `cancellingAnOrderCancelsItsCreatedShipments` verifies CREATED shipments are cancelled\nTests         `cancellingACancelledOrderSucceedsAndReturnsTheOrderUnchanged` verifies idempotency\nTests         `cancellingFailsWith409IfAnyShipmentIsCConfirmed` verifies atomicity — 409 thrown, order and shipment unchanged via separate GETs\nTests         `cancellingANonexistentOrderReturns404WithOrderNotFoundCode` verifies 404 with error code\nTests         `creatingAShipmentForACancelledOrderReturns409WithOrderCancelledCode` verifies shipment creation blocked with error code\nTests         `cancellingAnOrderWithMixedShipmentStatusesCancelsOnlyCreatedOnes` verifies only CREATED shipments are affected\nVerification  `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ returned: Tests run: 21, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0, BUILD SUCCESS\nNot done      (All requirements completed)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3341,"cache_read_input_tokens":33668,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3341},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7517c5a9-f734-4f39-9333-2e161584f361","uuid":"baec618f-a463-4dbd-af86-fbd0b45328e3","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:29:24.728Z","request_id":"req_011CetREv67AEaM9mBZjdoPL"}
